-- Enemy paths, one row per polyline point, in map (image-pixel) space matching
-- the level art. point_index is travel order: point 0 is the spawn, the last is
-- the exit.
--
-- Lexington and Concord (path 0): the British advance -- enters at "To Boston"
-- (right), follows the road west through the S-curve past Lexington Green, up to
-- Concord, and out across the Old North Bridge (left). Hand-traced route,
-- centered on the road (tower-slot platforms excluded), smoothed with a
-- centripetal Catmull-Rom spline and arc-length resampled to evenly spaced
-- points for smooth enemy walking. Traced from images/lexington_and_concord.png.

-- Bunker Hill (two paths converging on the American redoubt). Path 0 enters
-- at Charlestown Neck (north-west) and follows the neck road south past
-- Bunker Hill. Path 1 lands at Morton's Point (east) and crosses Morton's
-- Hill westward. Both end at the redoubt's south gate -- the historical
-- British assault geometry of June 17, 1775. Hand-traced on
-- images/level_002_bunker_hill.png, Catmull-Rom smoothed, resampled ~0.34px.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first ';'.)

-- Great Bridge (single path) on the painted art (1447x1087). The British
-- column enters top-right where the road crosses the playable rect edge,
-- crosses the long wooden bridge over the marsh, and follows the causeway
-- past the Culpeper Riflemen positions to the rect's bottom edge.
-- Hand-traced, Catmull-Rom smoothed, resampled ~0.34px.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first one.)

-- Moore's Creek Bridge (single path): the Loyalist column enters at the
-- north-west rect edge, marches the causeway road to the bridge, crosses
-- Moore's Creek, and pushes south-east past the patriot earthworks toward
-- the camp, exiting at the south-east rect edge. Hand-traced on
-- images/level_004_moores_creek_bridge.png, ~0.34px spacing.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first one.)

-- Long Island (three paths converging on Brooklyn Heights): path 0 is the
-- Flatbush Road east approach, path 1 the Jamaica Road center approach,
-- path 2 the Bedford Road south approach. Paths 1 and 2 merge at the
-- central junction and cross the Gowanus causeway to the works' south
-- side. Path 0 enters the works from the north-east. Hand-traced on the
-- repainted images/level_007_long_island.png, ~0.34px spacing.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first one.)

-- Trenton (two paths from the Delaware landing): path 0 skirts the town's
-- south edge and follows the east road down to the Sorentown/Bordentown
-- exit. Path 1 turns south, crosses the Assunpink stone bridge, and takes
-- the west road past Princeton Pond to the western exit. Hand-traced on
-- images/level_008_trenton.png, ~0.34px spacing.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first one.)

-- Princeton (two paths from the two British gates on the west edge): path 0
-- from the upper gate crosses the northern creek bridge and follows the
-- east road past the statue to the Continental standard by the campus
-- (the exit). Path 1 from the lower gate takes the southern road over the
-- lower bridge and climbs the field-edge road to the same exit.
-- Hand-traced on images/level_009_princeton.png, ~0.34px spacing.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first one.)

-- Charleston, the siege (two paths from the British siege lines at the neck
-- of the peninsula): path 0 takes the west road around the first bastion
-- and down the west side of the city. Path 1 takes the east road through
-- the fortification gates and straight down the city's central street.
-- Both end at the southern citadel. Hand-traced on
-- images/level_014_siege_of_charleston.png, ~0.34px spacing.
-- (No semicolons in these comments: block edits split on the first one.)
